{"id": "5b272548", "word": "pyre", "tweet1": {"text": "it's 2038. a new pandemic has swept the globe, deadlier than the last. my wife has ignited all my electronics in a pyre in the front yard because she read an article that said you can \u201ccontract the virus online\u201d. my love for her grows stronger with each passing day.", "tokens": ["it's", "2038", ".", "a", "new", "pandemic", "has", "swept", "the", "globe", ",", "deadlier", "than", "the", "last", ".", "my", "wife", "has", "ignited", "all", "my", "electronics", "in", "a", "pyre", "in", "the", "front", "yard", "because", "she", "read", "an", "article", "that", "said", "you", "can", "\u201c", "contract", "the", "virus", "online", "\u201d", ".", "my", "love", "for", "her", "grows", "stronger", "with", "each", "passing", "day", "."], "token_idx": 25, "text_start": 115, "text_end": 119, "date": "2020-04"}, "tweet2": {"text": "i can't believe that i used to write lines like \"if i was a crematorium my lover's name would be the first spark to the pyre\" jesus what happened to me and my poetry", "tokens": ["i", "can't", "believe", "that", "i", "used", "to", "write", "lines", "like", "\"", "if", "i", "was", "a", "crematorium", "my", "lover's", "name", "would", "be", "the", "first", "spark", "to", "the", "pyre", "\"", "jesus", "what", "happened", "to", "me", "and", "my", "poetry"], "token_idx": 26, "text_start": 120, "text_end": 124, "date": "2021-04"}}
