{"id": "c49bbcae", "word": "pyre", "tweet1": {"text": "Some people choose to see the ugliness in this world. I choose to see the beauty. Value those precious moments of empathy, remember the meaning of life. Even as the world burns to cinders like a pyre, be a beacon of hope, a guide in the dark, a lighthouse. I believe in you. \ud83d\udd25", "tokens": ["Some", "people", "choose", "to", "see", "the", "ugliness", "in", "this", "world", ".", "I", "choose", "to", "see", "the", "beauty", ".", "Value", "those", "precious", "moments", "of", "empathy", ",", "remember", "the", "meaning", "of", "life", ".", "Even", "as", "the", "world", "burns", "to", "cinders", "like", "a", "pyre", ",", "be", "a", "beacon", "of", "hope", ",", "a", "guide", "in", "the", "dark", ",", "a", "lighthouse", ".", "I", "believe", "in", "you", ".", "\ud83d\udd25"], "token_idx": 40, "text_start": 195, "text_end": 199, "date": "2020-04"}, "tweet2": {"text": "DelhiPolice ASI Rakesh 56yr old, father of 3, lives in PS Nizamuddin barrack. On duty at Lodi Road crematorium since 13 Apr, has helped over 1100 last rites, himself lit pyre for over 50. Postponed daughter's marriage due yesterday to attend to #covid duties #DilKiPolice #Heroes", "tokens": ["DelhiPolice", "ASI", "Rakesh", "56yr", "old", ",", "father", "of", "3", ",", "lives", "in", "PS", "Nizamuddin", "barrack", ".", "On", "duty", "at", "Lodi", "Road", "crematorium", "since", "13", "Apr", ",", "has", "helped", "over", "1100", "last", "rites", ",", "himself", "lit", "pyre", "for", "over", "50", ".", "Postponed", "daughter's", "marriage", "due", "yesterday", "to", "attend", "to", "#covid", "duties", "#DilKiPolice", "#Heroes"], "token_idx": 35, "text_start": 170, "text_end": 174, "date": "2021-04"}}
