{"id": "6382a586", "word": "pyre", "tweet1": {"text": "I am a Brahmin woman. First of all we don't go to the cremation grounds while alive. But even if allowed, why would daughter want to see her father being on the pyre. Isn't it extremely emotional? We women aren't prepared for such events. Men are prepared for it since childhood.", "tokens": ["I", "am", "a", "Brahmin", "woman", ".", "First", "of", "all", "we", "don't", "go", "to", "the", "cremation", "grounds", "while", "alive", ".", "But", "even", "if", "allowed", ",", "why", "would", "daughter", "want", "to", "see", "her", "father", "being", "on", "the", "pyre", ".", "Isn't", "it", "extremely", "emotional", "?", "We", "women", "aren't", "prepared", "for", "such", "events", ".", "Men", "are", "prepared", "for", "it", "since", "childhood", "."], "token_idx": 35, "text_start": 161, "text_end": 165, "date": "2020-04"}, "tweet2": {"text": "A friend shared a horrifying experience of cremating his uncle - 'Saumya, we used broken chairs, old doors, anything we could get our hands on to build the pyre, after waiting for 3 hours in a crematorium functioning at twice its capacity.' :(", "tokens": ["A", "friend", "shared", "a", "horrifying", "experience", "of", "cremating", "his", "uncle", "-", "'", "Saumya", ",", "we", "used", "broken", "chairs", ",", "old", "doors", ",", "anything", "we", "could", "get", "our", "hands", "on", "to", "build", "the", "pyre", ",", "after", "waiting", "for", "3", "hours", "in", "a", "crematorium", "functioning", "at", "twice", "its", "capacity", ".", "'", ":("], "token_idx": 32, "text_start": 156, "text_end": 160, "date": "2021-04"}}
